      {
        "id": 147068,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-07T05:34:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Wow. &nbsp;I tried this a couple of times, and it is brutal. &nbsp;I'm pretty sure that it is winnable, though.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Assuming all decks are stacked to make this winnable:</p><p>The simplest way to do it would be to bring out all the underbosses as fast as possible (Using Informants, Rook City is Mine, and Scum and Villany), and get the Chairman to reshuffle while all the Underbosses are in play. &nbsp;Then Oblivion them all to hell, and let Nightmist sacrifice herself (doing as much damage as she can on the way). &nbsp;Use Grease Guns to mitigate damage while the underbosses are in play. &nbsp;When the deck reshuffles, put both Thieves on top. &nbsp;One of DW Nightmist's incap abilities is to put the top card of a trash on top of that deck. &nbsp;So, an Aimed Hairtrigger Reflexes, combined with that ability can completely lock down the Chairman. &nbsp;While Expat is constantly Aiming, she's dropping guns for a finishing Unload, and Fixer is beating on his nemeses. &nbsp;You're limited by the size of the environment deck, but you should have plenty of time to take down the Chairman and the Operative. &nbsp;The only concern is the Operative damage from killing the thief over and over, and the Chairman's reaction damage, but those are both small enough that you should easily outpace them.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:25:06.126Z",
