      {
        "id": 147069,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-07T14:11:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This one is easier on advanced.&nbsp;<span>(or maybe more likely is more accurate)</span></p><p><span>Flip Chairman as fast as possible, and you need your redirection in play quickly.</span></p><p><span>From there you are trying to line up so that Operative damage goes to Chairman for retaliation, and Nightmist should always be set up to redirect a hitman shot to Chairman to clear the biggest threat.</span></p><p><span>Beyond that hope to heck that Rook City doesn't ruin everything.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
