      {
        "id": 147074,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-07T18:35:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Arcanist Lupus wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;When the deck reshuffles, put both Thieves on top. &nbsp;One of DW Nightmist's incap abilities is to put the top card of a trash on top of that deck. &nbsp;So, an Aimed Hairtrigger Reflexes, combined with that ability can completely lock down the Chairman. &nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI am thinking that Rook City won't let that situation last very long.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You might think so, but since we're stacking decks already, stack Rook City to give you Dr. Tremata, Tony Taurus, 2x Toxic Sludges, 3x Falling Statuary, and the Ambitious Racketeer, and you can last quite a while before your lock breaks.</p>",
